SYNTHETIC – 8.1 entry whose queue row reports a data stream of 10,485,761 bytes (one
byte over 10 MiB); there is no .data file, as the data stream is never requested. Expected:
only the variables are requested (no data output path); data unavailable with the reason
"too large (10485761 bytes; limit 10 MiB)"; variables read.

Frames use the fixed nonce 0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef; a replay replaces it with the
nonce of its request. Lines without the frame prefix are vendor noise the classifier ignores.
Used by QueueEntryV81ContractTest (tasks.md T026, research D-18, D-19).
